    "note": [
      "[b]Worry about crime \r\n\r\n[/b] [b]How do we measure this?[/b] \r\nPercentage of people who, when thinking about all types of crime in general, are very worried about being a victim of crime.\r\n\r\n[b]Source[/b] \r\nNorthern Ireland Safe Community Telephone Survey\r\n[url=https://www.justice-ni.gov.uk/articles/findings-northern-ireland-safe-community-telephone-survey]https://www.justice-ni.gov.uk/articles/findings-northern-ireland-safe-community-telephone-survey[/url]\r\n\r\n[b]Impact of Covid-19[/b]\r\nThere was a change in survey mode from 2020/21 due to the pandemic and the method by which interviews were undertaken changed from face-to-face to telephone. This resulted in a break in the time series. Results for the four latest years, 2020/21 to 2023/24, are not directly comparable with previous sweeps. The change also reduced the sample size for the first two years, particularly in 2020/21.\r\n\r\n[b]Further information[/b] \r\n1. The Northern Ireland Safe Community Survey was previously known as the NI Crime Survey. Given the change in survey mode as a result of the pandemic, the survey years from 2020/21 are referenced as the Northern Ireland Safe Community Telephone Survey. \r\n2. Previously conducted on an ad hoc basis, the survey began operating on a continuous basis in January 2005.\r\n3. Data are not available for 2006/07 as the question was only asked from 2007/08.\r\n4. Results exclude don't knows and refusals."
